Contains the header and sources files from selected xcb libraries:

   libxcb-1.5 together with xcb-proto-1.6 (sync, xfixes, randr, xinerama sources)
   # libxkbcommon-x11 requires libxcb-xkb >= 1.10
   libxcb-1.10 together with xcb-proto-1.10 (xkb sources)
   libxcb-util-image-0.3.9
   libxcb-util-keysyms-0.3.9
   libxcb-util-renderutil-0.3.8
   libxcb-util-wm-0.3.9

The 'include' directory was obtained by compiling and installing all of the modules.
They have been tested to run also with libxcb 1.5 (the oldest version we support).

Use the -qt-xcb configure option to use the files instead of system xcb libraries.
See src/plugins/platforms/xcb/README for details.

Core XCB and Xau sources are bundled so the XCB backend does not link the system libxcb or libXau:

libxcb-core:
      Source: https://xorg.freedesktop.org/archive/individual/lib/libxcb-1.14.tar.xz
      Version: 1.14
      Generated protocol sources and headers use xcb-proto 1.14.1:
      https://xorg.freedesktop.org/archive/individual/proto/xcb-proto-1.14.1.tar.xz
   libxau:
      Source: https://xorg.freedesktop.org/archive/individual/lib/libXau-1.0.9.tar.bz2
      Version: 1.0.9

The generated xproto.c/xproto.h, bigreq.c/bigreq.h, and xc_misc.c/xc_misc.h
are included in libxcb-core/src and libxcb-core/include/xcb; generation is not
required when building LeanQt. HASXDMAUTH is not defined, so libXdmcp is not
needed. The Xau authentication routines used by libxcb are built from the
bundled libXau sources; its optional lock/unlock routines are not needed by
libxcb. The checked-in libxcb-core/src/config.h freezes the upstream
configure defaults for XCB_QUEUE_BUFFER_SIZE (16384) and its IOV_MAX fallback (16).

Protocol and cursor headers needed by the XCB backend are bundled instead of copied into the target sysroot:

   Source: https://xorg.freedesktop.org/archive/individual/proto/xorgproto-2021.5.tar.bz2
   Version: 2021.5

The minimal X11 compatibility headers needed by the bundled libXau build and
the XCB cursor glyph names are from Ubuntu's libx11-dev 2:1.7.5-1ubuntu0.4
package. They do not add any Xlib linkage. 
